  "2": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.51a.3",
   "sugya": "berakhot_50b_shachach_vehichnis",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_halach_rav_chisda",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "הלכך -- therefore [from Rav Chisda's answer], even if he finished his meal he goes back and blesses",
     "supports": "p_afilu_gamar_seudato",
     "status": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "support",
     "object": "s_detanya_tevila",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "דתניא: טבל ועלה, אומר בעלייתו ברוך... על הטבילה -- a blessing may be said after the act is complete",
     "supports": "p_afilu_gamar_seudato",
     "status": "rejected"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_afilu_gamar_seudato",
     "gloss_en": "Ravina: therefore, even if he finished his meal, he goes back and blesses"
    }
   ]
  },
  "3": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.51a.4",
   "sugya": "berakhot_50b_shachach_vehichnis",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "support_deflection",
     "object": "defl_hatam_lo_chazi",
     "gloss_en": "ולא היא: התם מעיקרא גברא לא חזי -- there, before immersing, the man was not fit to bless at all; the case does not transfer",
     "deflects": "s_detanya_tevila",
     "refuted": false
    },
    {
     "type": "objection",
     "object": "obj_vela_hi",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "ולא היא: ...הכא מעיקרא גברא חזי, והואיל ואידחי אידחי -- one who was fit to bless and let the moment pass has been pushed aside for good",
     "against": "p_afilu_gamar_seudato",
     "state": "live"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_hoil_veidchi",
     "gloss_en": "the stam: here, from the start the man was fit [to bless], and since he was pushed aside, he is pushed aside"
    }
   ]
  },
  "0": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.51a.1",
   "sugya": "berakhot_50b_shachach_vehichnis",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "objection",
     "object": "obj_lesalkinhu",
     "kind": "svara",
     "gloss_en": "במידי דלא ממאיס נמי, לסלקינהו לצד אחד וליברך! -- with a thing that does not become repulsive too, let him move it aside and bless",
     "against": "p_poltan_belo_mimeis",
     "state": "answered"
    },
    {
     "type": "objection_answer",
     "object": "a_yimale_fi",
     "gloss_en": "משום שנאמר ימלא פי תהלתך -- the mouth must be filled with the praise (= p_yimale_fi; transmitted by Rav Yitzchak Kaskesa'a)",
     "answers": "obj_lesalkinhu",
     "restores": "p_poltan_belo_mimeis"
    },
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_yimale_fi",
     "gloss_en": "R' Yochanan: [he spits it out] because it is said 'my mouth shall be filled with Your praise' (Ps 71:8)"
    }
   ]
  },
  "1": {
   "segId": "Berakhot.51a.2",
   "sugya": "berakhot_50b_shachach_vehichnis",
   "marks": [
    {
     "type": "proposition",
     "object": "p_chozer_umevarech",
     "gloss_en": "Rav Chisda, answering 'one who ate and drank and did not bless -- may he go back and bless?': one who ate garlic and his breath smells -- shall he go back and eat more garlic so that his breath smells?! [i.e., he goes back and blesses]"
    }
   ]
  },
  "5": {
